// Module c-neuro-oncology: primary and metastatic brain tumors. How tumors present, contrast
// MRI and the imaging patterns that suggest a diagnosis, the ring-enhancing differential,
// tissue diagnosis (and holding corticosteroids when lymphoma is possible), the 2021 WHO
// classification at a principles level, and the common complications: edema, seizures,
// venous thromboembolism, and leptomeningeal disease. Paraneoplastic syndromes and spinal
// cord compression have their own modules. Doses are deliberately left out.

